1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:03,562
Order a 25,000-won fried chicken,

2
00:00:03,562 --> 00:00:05,800
and the owner keeps 3,037 won.

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:11,330
The delivery app takes more than twice that: about 6,700 won.

4
00:00:12,130 --> 00:00:12,946
Strangely,

5
00:00:12,946 --> 00:00:17,350
the app's own profit has been shrinking for two years.

6
00:00:18,150 --> 00:00:19,709
And right now,

7
00:00:19,709 --> 00:00:26,390
Uber is trying to buy the company that owns Baemin outright.

8
00:00:27,190 --> 00:00:30,300
Why more hands share the same chicken money,

9
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,410
and how to save 2,000 won tonight. Let's go.

10
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:38,490
Part one: let's cut this delivery bag in half.

11
00:00:39,290 --> 00:00:44,615
Asia Economy broke down one 25,000-won chicken in Seoul,

12
00:00:44,615 --> 00:00:49,180
at the top 7.8% commission tier and with no ads.

13
00:00:49,380 --> 00:00:52,467
First, 2,273 won of VAT goes to the government.

14
00:00:52,467 --> 00:00:54,240
One drumstick already gone.

15
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:58,123
Next, the app: 1,950 won commission,

16
00:00:58,123 --> 00:01:01,635
3,400 won delivery fee paid by the owner,

17
00:01:01,635 --> 00:01:04,890
750 won card fee, plus VAT: 6,710 won.

18
00:01:05,090 --> 00:01:06,005
One chicken,

19
00:01:06,005 --> 00:01:09,130
and already three parties are sharing it.

20
00:01:09,930 --> 00:01:13,387
But the biggest slice isn't the app: chicken,

21
00:01:13,387 --> 00:01:13,694
oil,

22
00:01:13,694 --> 00:01:18,380
sauce and boxes bought from the franchise HQ cost 11,480 won,

23
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:20,070
nearly half the price.

24
00:01:20,870 --> 00:01:24,529
Take out about 1,500 won for rent and part-time wages,

25
00:01:24,529 --> 00:01:26,020
and 3,037 won is left.

26
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:29,040
And that's before the owner's own labor,

27
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:30,450
electricity and gas.

28
00:01:31,250 --> 00:01:36,532
Add ads and it changes again: 200 to 600 won per click,

29
00:01:36,532 --> 00:01:40,950
pushing platform costs up to 40% of the order.

30
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:44,106
That answers the first question,

31
00:01:44,106 --> 00:01:46,516
where the 25,000 won goes.

32
00:01:46,516 --> 00:01:49,390
So how many restaurants closed?

33
00:01:51,090 --> 00:01:51,753
Part two,

34
00:01:51,753 --> 00:01:55,069
the street in numbers: in 2024 over 1,008,000

35
00:01:55,069 --> 00:01:56,985
businesses filed to close,

36
00:01:56,985 --> 00:01:59,270
the first time above a million.

37
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:03,165
In 2025, another 975,000 closed,

38
00:02:03,165 --> 00:02:06,250
142,557 of them in food service.

39
00:02:06,450 --> 00:02:10,230
That's about 390 restaurants pulling down the shutter every day.

40
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:17,601
A Seoul survey tracked 186 franchise shops for

41
00:02:17,601 --> 00:02:25,600
a year: fees rose from 17.1% to 24.0% of delivery sales.

42
00:02:25,790 --> 00:02:30,572
Chicken shops' operating margin was 6.5%,

43
00:02:30,572 --> 00:02:35,820
meaning 6.5 won left from every 100 won sold.

44
00:02:36,630 --> 00:02:38,282
While shops were closing like this,

45
00:02:38,282 --> 00:02:40,170
how did the side collecting the fees do?

46
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:45,714
Part three: Woowa Brothers, Baemin's operator.

47
00:02:45,714 --> 00:02:47,642
Revenue grew 1.5 times,

48
00:02:47,642 --> 00:02:52,250
from 3.4 trillion won in 2023 to 5.28 trillion in 2025.

49
00:02:53,050 --> 00:02:56,294
Closures rose, yet app revenue grew,

50
00:02:56,294 --> 00:02:59,628
because the app earns on every order,

51
00:02:59,628 --> 00:03:00,980
not every shop.

52
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:05,121
If chicken shop A closes and the customer orders from shop B,

53
00:03:05,121 --> 00:03:06,607
the fee still comes in.

54
00:03:06,607 --> 00:03:09,773
Even in the year closures first topped a million,

55
00:03:09,773 --> 00:03:11,130
app revenue rose 26%.

56
00:03:11,930 --> 00:03:16,878
But here's the twist: operating profit went the other way,

57
00:03:16,878 --> 00:03:19,778
699.8 billion, then 640.8 billion,

58
00:03:19,778 --> 00:03:21,740
then 592.9 billion won.

59
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:25,450
Revenue grew 1.5 times while profit fell two years in a row.

60
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:29,274
Meanwhile the two apps went head to head:

61
00:03:29,274 --> 00:03:31,855
Coupang Eats offered free delivery,

62
00:03:31,855 --> 00:03:33,330
and Baemin followed.

63
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:34,087
In July,

64
00:03:34,087 --> 00:03:38,465
Baemin had 23 million monthly users and Coupang Eats 13 million,

65
00:03:38,465 --> 00:03:41,270
two apps spending to win the same people.

66
00:03:42,070 --> 00:03:45,671
When customers are the same,

67
00:03:45,671 --> 00:03:53,260
the fight is fought with money: who pays for free delivery.

68
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:56,594
So what's the surest way to end this fight?

69
00:03:56,594 --> 00:04:00,020
An American company coming up shows the answer.

70
00:04:01,720 --> 00:04:07,043
Before that, the biggest slice of the bag.

71
00:04:07,043 --> 00:04:11,860
Part four: the franchise headquarters.

72
00:04:12,660 --> 00:04:17,232
HQs earn three ways: franchise and training fees at opening,

73
00:04:17,232 --> 00:04:20,280
interior work, and a margin on supplies.

74
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:22,879
That third one is the supply markup: the gap

75
00:04:22,879 --> 00:04:26,260
between what HQ pays for chicken and what it charges the shop.

76
00:04:27,060 --> 00:04:29,301
By the Fair Trade Commission's count,

77
00:04:29,301 --> 00:04:32,147
chicken HQs earned an average 41 million won in

78
00:04:32,147 --> 00:04:34,024
supply markup per shop in 2024,

79
00:04:34,024 --> 00:04:35,720
the most of any food sector.

80
00:04:35,930 --> 00:04:39,398
Without frying a single chicken,

81
00:04:39,398 --> 00:04:44,600
about an office worker's annual salary per shop.

82
00:04:45,390 --> 00:04:47,756
Courts are involved too: in January,

83
00:04:47,756 --> 00:04:50,714
Korea's Supreme Court ordered Pizza Hut Korea

84
00:04:50,714 --> 00:04:54,460
to return 21.5 billion won taken without owners' consent.

85
00:04:54,660 --> 00:04:57,760
Owners of about 20 chicken and pizza brands,

86
00:04:57,760 --> 00:05:00,860
including Kyochon, have filed similar suits.

87
00:05:00,860 --> 00:05:05,440
HQ earns every time supplies move; owners keep only what is left.

88
00:05:07,140 --> 00:05:10,340
Part five, back to the earlier question.

89
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:14,740
The surest way to end a delivery-app fight is to merge.

90
00:05:15,540 --> 00:05:17,794
DoorDash, America's top delivery app,

91
00:05:17,794 --> 00:05:20,170
closed its Deliveroo deal last October,

92
00:05:20,170 --> 00:05:22,546
and in late October announced a roughly

93
00:05:22,546 --> 00:05:24,800
17-billion-dollar deal for Instacart.

94
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:30,156
Uber went bigger: in July it offered 41.50 euros a share,

95
00:05:30,156 --> 00:05:32,313
about 14.8 billion dollars,

96
00:05:32,313 --> 00:05:35,830
for Germany's Delivery Hero, Baemin's owner.

97
00:05:36,030 --> 00:05:39,354
Delivery Hero owns essentially 100% of Woowa.

98
00:05:39,354 --> 00:05:40,757
If the deal closes,

99
00:05:40,757 --> 00:05:44,229
chicken fried in Seoul could show up as fees in

100
00:05:44,229 --> 00:05:46,740
a San Francisco company's results.

101
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:50,426
It's not the first time. In December 2020,

102
00:05:50,426 --> 00:05:53,518
the KFTC approved Delivery Hero's purchase of

103
00:05:53,518 --> 00:05:56,060
Baemin on one condition: sell Yogiyo,

104
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,640
which it already owned.

105
00:05:57,840 --> 00:06:00,145
If No.1 and No.2 share a roof,

106
00:06:00,145 --> 00:06:02,988
there's nowhere to go when fees rise.

107
00:06:02,988 --> 00:06:04,063
This time too,

108
00:06:04,063 --> 00:06:07,060
the KFTC began its review in September.

109
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:09,958
So is Uber, ready to spend this much,

110
00:06:09,958 --> 00:06:12,000
expensive against what it earns now?

111
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,040
By ValueNote,

112
00:06:13,040 --> 00:06:16,014
which scores companies on Warren Buffett's and

113
00:06:16,014 --> 00:06:17,824
Benjamin Graham's standards,

114
00:06:17,824 --> 00:06:20,604
Uber scores 39 out of 100: 57 for financial

115
00:06:20,604 --> 00:06:23,901
strength and 30 for price against current earnings.

116
00:06:23,901 --> 00:06:25,582
The lower the price score,

117
00:06:25,582 --> 00:06:28,620
the more future hopes are already in the stock.

118
00:06:30,320 --> 00:06:36,680
Going a bit deeper: the 7.8% you often hear is only the commission.

119
00:06:37,480 --> 00:06:39,089
Add card fees,

120
00:06:39,089 --> 00:06:44,374
delivery and ads and you get the total fee: on

121
00:06:44,374 --> 00:06:48,970
average 26.2% of a shop's monthly sales.

122
00:06:49,170 --> 00:06:52,751
Three bills in the National Assembly would cap

123
00:06:52,751 --> 00:06:57,810
the total at 15%; as of mid-October they were still in committee.

124
00:06:58,610 --> 00:07:00,647
A cap would ease owners' costs,

125
00:07:00,647 --> 00:07:02,946
but critics say platforms could cut

126
00:07:02,946 --> 00:07:06,560
free-delivery support and pass costs back to customers.

127
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:09,217
In the end it's a tug of war over who keeps how

128
00:07:09,217 --> 00:07:10,680
much of the same 25,000 won.

129
00:07:12,380 --> 00:07:13,066
Last part,

130
00:07:13,066 --> 00:07:16,153
something for tonight: the same chicken often

131
00:07:16,153 --> 00:07:19,240
costs differently in the app and in the shop.

132
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:23,558
A consumer group checked 29 franchises: 20

133
00:07:23,558 --> 00:07:25,736
charged more for delivery,

134
00:07:25,736 --> 00:07:28,500
about 2,000 won more per chicken.

135
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:31,217
Kyochon too raised Seoul app prices by 2,000

136
00:07:31,217 --> 00:07:32,590
won from last September.

137
00:07:33,390 --> 00:07:34,670
So before ordering,

138
00:07:34,670 --> 00:07:38,309
compare the app's delivery price with the shop's menu.

139
00:07:38,309 --> 00:07:39,455
If it's walkable,

140
00:07:39,455 --> 00:07:42,487
picking up yourself is better for your wallet

141
00:07:42,487 --> 00:07:43,970
and the owner's share.

142
00:07:44,170 --> 00:07:47,256
Even app pickup carries a 6.8% fee,

143
00:07:47,256 --> 00:07:50,960
but the 3,400-won delivery fee disappears.

144
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:54,897
And to see how the 25,000-won split changes from here,

145
00:07:54,897 --> 00:07:56,350
watch these three things.

146
00:07:57,140 --> 00:08:00,389
One: Uber's tender offer closing November 5.

147
00:08:00,389 --> 00:08:02,604
If more than half is tendered,

148
00:08:02,604 --> 00:08:04,671
Baemin's owner could change,

149
00:08:04,671 --> 00:08:06,960
and then comes the KFTC review.

150
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:10,460
Two: when the committee takes up the 15% cap

151
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:14,660
bills; you can track them on the Assembly's bill system.

152
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:19,277
Three: Woowa's 2026 audit report on DART next April,

153
00:08:19,277 --> 00:08:22,580
showing whether profit falls a third year and

154
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:25,590
whether the free-delivery war has cooled.

155
00:08:25,790 --> 00:08:28,824
In one line: chicken prices stayed,

156
00:08:28,824 --> 00:08:30,732
more hands share them,

157
00:08:30,732 --> 00:08:34,720
and the fight over the shares has gone global.

158
00:08:35,510 --> 00:08:38,104
If you want more stories about where money flows,

159
00:08:38,104 --> 00:08:40,380
please subscribe and turn on notifications.

160
00:08:40,580 --> 00:08:43,237
For another structure where an app earns from

161
00:08:43,237 --> 00:08:44,537
the money it collects,

162
00:08:44,537 --> 00:08:46,190
watch our Starbucks episode.

163
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:48,763
Tell us in the comments how much the app and

164
00:08:48,763 --> 00:08:51,233
shop prices differed for your chicken tonight.

165
00:08:51,233 --> 00:08:51,770
Thank you.
